6
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:16,976
Rachel:
ALL RIGHT.

7
00:00:17,017 --> 00:00:19,186
WHOSE ARE THEY?

8
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:20,354
WHOSE ARE THEY?

9
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:21,355
NOT MINE.

10
00:00:21,396 --> 00:00:22,356
WELL, THEY'RE JOEY'S.

11
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:23,440
THEY GOT TO BE JOEY'S.

12
00:00:27,903 --> 00:00:29,321
YEAH, THEY'RE MINE.

13
00:00:29,363 --> 00:00:30,489
SEE, JOEY'S.

14
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:32,700
THEY'RE J-J-J-J-JOEY'S.

15
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:34,451
WHY ARE THEY HERE?

16
00:00:34,493 --> 00:00:36,704
I DON'T KNOW, UH...

17
00:00:38,372 --> 00:00:39,874
I'M JOEY.

18
00:00:41,709 --> 00:00:42,918
YEAH, I'M DISGUSTING.

19
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,879
I TAKE MY UNDERWEAR OFF
IN OTHER PEOPLE'S HOMES.

20
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:48,883
WELL, GET 'EM OUT OF HERE.

21
00:00:48,924 --> 00:00:50,342
WHAT'S WRONG WITH YOU?

22
00:00:50,384 --> 00:00:51,426
YEAH.
YEAH.

23
00:00:53,971 --> 00:00:55,055
TAKE 'EM.

24
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:56,515
OH, I GOT...

25
00:00:56,557 --> 00:00:57,975
JOEY, YOU CAN TOUCH THEM.

26
00:00:58,017 --> 00:00:59,393
THEY'RE YOUR UNDERWEAR.

27
00:01:03,898 --> 00:01:06,233
CHANDLER, A WORD?

28
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:07,651
YEAH.

29
00:01:13,991 --> 00:01:15,200
THAT'S IT.

30
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:16,952
I'M TIRED OF COVERING
FOR YOU TWO.

31
00:01:16,994 --> 00:01:18,037
THIS HAS GOT TO STOP.

32
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:19,079
UGH!

33
00:01:20,581 --> 00:01:21,665
AND TIGHTY-WHITEYS?

34
00:01:21,707 --> 00:01:22,917
WHAT ARE YOU, EIGHT?

35
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:26,003
THANK YOU, JOEY.
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

36
00:01:26,045 --> 00:01:28,255
WELL, HEY, NO,
YOU'RE NOT WELCOME, OKAY?

37
00:01:28,296 --> 00:01:29,381
LOOK, I HATE THIS.

38
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:31,216
YOU GUYS KEEP EMBARRASSING ME.

39
00:01:31,258 --> 00:01:34,302
YESTERDAY, RACHEL FOUND
YOUR RAZOR IN OUR BATHROOM.

40
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:35,846
I DIDN'T KNOW WHAT TO SAY

41
00:01:35,888 --> 00:01:37,890
SO I SAID IT WAS MINE
AND... AND...

42
00:01:37,932 --> 00:01:40,392
AND THAT I WAS PLAYING
A WOMAN IN A PLAY.

43
00:01:41,936 --> 00:01:45,272
AND, WELL, ONE THING
LED TO ANOTHER AND...

44
00:01:49,777 --> 00:01:51,278
WOW, AND AROUND THE ANKLES.

45
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:52,863
YOU KNOW, THAT
IS A TOUGH SPOT.

46
00:01:52,905 --> 00:01:53,864
YEAH, IT WAS.

47
00:01:53,906 --> 00:01:55,365
ALL RIGHT, LISTEN,
I CAN'T...

48
00:01:55,407 --> 00:01:57,576
ALL THIS LYING HAS BEEN
HARD ON US, TOO.

49
00:01:57,618 --> 00:02:00,287
OH, YEAH, I BET ALL THE SEX
MAKES IT EASIER.

50
00:02:01,956 --> 00:02:03,749
WELL, YEAH, ACTUALLY.

51
00:02:05,042 --> 00:02:06,668
WE'LL TRY TO BE
MORE CAREFUL, OKAY?

52
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:07,711
IT'S JUST THAT...

53
00:02:07,753 --> 00:02:09,088
WE DON'T WANT
EVERYONE TO KNOW

54
00:02:09,128 --> 00:02:10,672
BECAUSE THIS IS
GOING REALLY WELL.

55
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:12,257
AND MAYBE
THE REASON

56
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:15,343
IT'S GOING REALLY WELL IS...
IS BECAUSE IT'S A SECRET.

57
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:17,262
I KNOW IT SOUNDS
REALLY WEIRD

58
00:02:17,304 --> 00:02:19,598
BUT WE'RE JUST BOTH
SO BAD AT RELATIONSHIPS.

59
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:20,849
WE ARE. HELP US.

60
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:23,477
ALL RIGHT.

61
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:26,105
BUT YOU DO IT WITH ME ONCE.

62
00:02:29,984 --> 00:02:31,234
JOEY.

63
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:32,527
DIDN'T THINK SO.

64
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:45,290
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

65
00:02:45,332 --> 00:02:47,668
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

66
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:50,629
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

67
00:02:50,671 --> 00:02:55,050
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

68
00:02:55,092 --> 00:02:57,970
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

69
00:02:58,012 --> 00:03:00,014
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

70
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:03,642
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

71
00:03:03,684 --> 00:03:05,769
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

72
00:03:05,811 --> 00:03:08,355
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

73
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:10,607
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

74
00:03:10,649 --> 00:03:13,819
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

75
00:03:13,861 --> 00:03:17,196
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

76
00:03:24,163 --> 00:03:25,204
HEY, PHOEBE.

77
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:26,247
HI, PHEEBS.

78
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:28,042
WHAT ARE
YOU READING?

79
00:03:28,083 --> 00:03:29,543
WUTHERING HEIGHTS.

80
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:31,419
I'M TAKING A LITERATURE CLASS
AT THE NEW SCHOOL

81
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:34,006
AND I HAVE TO FINISH IT
FOR THE FIRST SESSION TOMORROW.

82
00:03:34,048 --> 00:03:36,633
I DIDN'T KNOW YOU WERE
TAKING A CLASS.
THAT'S SO COOL.

83
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:39,386
YEAH, WELL, I REALLY LIKED
THAT LAMAZE CLASS I TOOK

84
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:41,471
YOU KNOW, AND I JUST THOUGHT
THIS TIME

85
00:03:41,513 --> 00:03:44,641
I'D GO FOR SOMETHING, YOU KNOW,
A LITTLE MORE INTELLECTUAL

86
00:03:44,683 --> 00:03:46,393
WITH A LESS PAINFUL FINAL EXAM.

87
00:03:46,434 --> 00:03:48,395
HONEY, THAT
SOUNDS LIKE FUN.

88
00:03:48,436 --> 00:03:49,396
YEAH.

89
00:03:49,437 --> 00:03:51,773
OH, YOU SHOULD
COME WITH ME.

90
00:03:51,815 --> 00:03:54,193
OH, YEAH, THEN I'LL HAVE SOMEONE
TO SIT WITH.

91
00:03:54,233 --> 00:03:55,194
OKAY.

92
00:03:55,234 --> 00:03:56,486
YAY! OKAY.

93
00:03:56,528 --> 00:03:58,279
BUT ARE YOU GOING
TO HAVE TIME TO READ IT?

94
00:03:58,321 --> 00:03:59,614
I READ THAT
IN HIGH SCHOOL.

95
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:01,783
OH, THIS IS GOING TO BE
SO MUCH FUN.

96
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:03,702
OKAY, SHH. I HAVE TO FINISH.

97
00:04:07,748 --> 00:04:08,957
HI.

98
00:04:08,999 --> 00:04:10,250
HI.

99
00:04:10,291 --> 00:04:11,459
WHAT'S WRONG, BUDDY?

100
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:14,088
SOMEONE AT WORK ATE MY SANDWICH.

101
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:18,133
WELL, WHAT DID
THE POLICE SAY?

102
00:04:18,175 --> 00:04:21,053
MY THANKSGIVING LEFTOVER
SANDWICH.

103
00:04:21,095 --> 00:04:24,181
I CAN'T BELIEVE
SOMEONE JUST ATE IT.

104
00:04:24,223 --> 00:04:25,640
ROSS, IT'S JUST
A SANDWICH.

105
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:27,101
JUST A SANDWICH?

106
00:04:27,142 --> 00:04:29,644
LOOK, I AM 30 YEARS OLD,
OKAY?

107
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:32,814
I'M GOING BE DIVORCED TWICE,
AND I JUST GOT EVICTED.

108
00:04:32,856 --> 00:04:36,484
THAT SANDWICH WAS THE ONLY
GOOD THING GOING ON IN MY LIFE.

109
00:04:36,526 --> 00:04:39,738
SOMEONE ATE THE ONLY GOOD THING
GOING ON IN MY LIFE.

110
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:42,824
OKAY, LOOK, I
HAVE ENOUGH STUFF

111
00:04:42,866 --> 00:04:44,159
FOR ONE MORE SANDWICH.

112
00:04:44,201 --> 00:04:46,870
I MEAN, I WAS GOING
TO EAT IT MYSELF, BUT...

113
00:04:46,912 --> 00:04:49,957
MON, TH-THAT WOULD BE
INCREDIBLE.

114
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:51,499
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

115
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:55,212
BUT I STILL CAN'T BELIEVE
SOMEONE ATE IT.

116
00:04:57,214 --> 00:04:59,633
I MEAN, LOOK, I LEFT A NOTE
AND EVERYTHING.

117
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:00,842
"KNOCK KNOCK.

118
00:05:00,884 --> 00:05:02,136
"WHO'S THERE?

119
00:05:02,177 --> 00:05:04,138
"ROSS GELLER'S LUNCH.

120
00:05:04,179 --> 00:05:06,681
"ROSS GELLER'S LUNCH, WHO?

121
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:11,311
ROSS GELLER'S LUNCH, PLEASE
DON'T TAKE ME, OKAY?"

122
00:05:12,646 --> 00:05:15,315
I'M SURPRISED YOU DIDN'T GO HOME
WEARING YOUR LUNCH.

123
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:16,984
Phoebe:
OKAY, LOOK

124
00:05:17,025 --> 00:05:18,401
YOU WANT TO HOLD ON
TO YOUR FOOD?

125
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:19,861
YOU'VE GOT TO SCARE PEOPLE OFF.

126
00:05:19,903 --> 00:05:21,529
I LEARNED THAT LIVING
ON THE STREET.

127
00:05:21,571 --> 00:05:22,864
REALLY?

128
00:05:22,906 --> 00:05:25,617
SO, WHAT WOULD YOU SAY, PHEEBS?

129
00:05:25,659 --> 00:05:29,621
STUFF LIKE, UH, "KEEP YOUR MITTS
OFF MY GRUB"?

130
00:05:31,123 --> 00:05:33,583
SAY, ROSS, WHEN YOU PICTURE
PHOEBE LIVING ON THE STREET

131
00:05:33,625 --> 00:05:35,752
IS SHE SURROUNDED
BY THE ENTIRE CAST OF ANNIE?

132
00:05:37,254 --> 00:05:40,299
OKAY, THIS'LL KEEP THEM
AWAY FROM YOUR STUFF.

133
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:45,553
OH.
WHOA.
JEEZ.

134
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:47,555
WHOA.

135
00:05:47,597 --> 00:05:49,724
PHOEBE, YOU ARE A BADASS.

136
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:53,812
SOMEDAY, I'LL TELL YOU ABOUT
THE TIME I STABBED A COP.

137
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:54,688
PHOEBE?

138
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:56,523
WHAT? HE STABBED ME FIRST.

139
00:06:00,443 --> 00:06:03,280
SEE, THE BRONTE SISTERS WERE
REALLY REMARKABLE WOMEN

140
00:06:03,322 --> 00:06:04,489
FOR THEIR TIME.

141
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:06,241
THEY LIVED IN A
PATRIARCHAL SOCIETY...

142
00:06:06,283 --> 00:06:08,743
SORRY I'M LATE,
BUT I LEFT LATE.

143
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:11,579
OKAY.

144
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:14,333
PHEEBS, WHAT IS
THE BOOK ABOUT?

145
00:06:14,373 --> 00:06:16,335
YOU SAID YOU READ IT
IN HIGH SCHOOL.

146
00:06:16,375 --> 00:06:18,128
YEAH, BUT I
REMEMBERED
I STARTED IT

147
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:19,880
BUT THEN THERE WAS
THIS PEP RALLY

148
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:21,589
AND I WAS ON TOP
OF THE PYRAMID.

149
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:24,843
ANYWAY, WHAT'S
THIS BOOK ABOUT?

150
00:06:24,885 --> 00:06:27,095
OKAY, IT'S THIS
TRAGIC LOVE STORY

151
00:06:27,137 --> 00:06:29,097
BETWEEN CATHY
AND HEATHCLIFF.

152
00:06:29,139 --> 00:06:33,143
AND IT TAKES PLACE ON
THESE REALLY CREEPY
MOORS IN ENGLAND.

153
00:06:33,185 --> 00:06:35,603
WHICH I THINK REPRESENT
THE WILDNESS

154
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:37,480
OF HEATHCLIFF'S CHARACTER.

155
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:39,191
I TOTALLY GET SYMBOLISM.

156
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:43,945
HOW WOULD YOU CHARACTERIZE
THE THEME OF THIS BOOK?

157
00:06:43,987 --> 00:06:45,989
UH, LET'S SEE...
RACHEL GREEN?

158
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:52,704
UH, WELL, I WOULD
HAVE TO SAY

159
00:06:52,746 --> 00:06:55,790
THAT IT'S A
TRAGIC LOVE STORY.

160
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:59,418
WELL, THAT'S SORT
OF A GIVEN, BUT... YES.

161
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:00,461
ANYONE ELSE?

162
00:07:00,503 --> 00:07:01,671
OH, OH, OH.

163
00:07:01,713 --> 00:07:04,341
SYMBOLISM, AND
THE, UH...

164
00:07:04,383 --> 00:07:06,676
WILDNESS OF THE MOORS

165
00:07:06,718 --> 00:07:11,139
WHICH I THINK IS
MIRRORED IN THE WILDNESS

166
00:07:11,181 --> 00:07:14,101
OF HEATHCLIFF'S CHARACTER.

167
00:07:15,602 --> 00:07:16,978
EXCELLENT.

168
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:19,647
WHAT RACHEL HAS SHREWDLY
OBSERVED HERE

169
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:20,982
IS AT THE HEART...

170
00:07:21,024 --> 00:07:23,026
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU STOLE
MY ANSWER.

171
00:07:23,068 --> 00:07:25,028
I THOUGHT IT WAS
PRETTY OBVIOUS.

172
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,154
HOW WOULD YOU KNOW?

173
00:07:26,196 --> 00:07:27,530
YOU DIDN'T EVEN READ IT.

174
00:07:29,366 --> 00:07:30,742
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

175
00:07:30,784 --> 00:07:32,953
UH, YOU, IN THE BLUE SHIRT.

176
00:07:34,829 --> 00:07:37,958
I THINK THAT YOURS
IS A QUESTION

177
00:07:37,999 --> 00:07:40,668
WITH MANY
POSSIBLE ANSWERS.

178
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:43,380
WOULD YOU CARE TO VENTURE ONE?

179
00:07:43,422 --> 00:07:47,342
WOULD YOU CARE
TO VENTURE ONE?

180
00:07:47,384 --> 00:07:49,803
ARE YOU JUST REPEATING
WHAT I'M SAYING?

181
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:53,098
ARE YOU JUST REPEATING
WHAT I'M SAYING?

182
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:54,433
ALL RIGHT.

183
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,351
LET'S MOVE ON.

184
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:58,312
OKAY, THEN.

185
00:08:02,357 --> 00:08:05,319
WHY DIDN'T YOU JUST SAY
THAT YOU HADN'T READ THE BOOK?

186
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,778
BECAUSE I DIDN'T
WANT HIM

187
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:07,946
TO THINK
I WAS STUPID.

188
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:09,781
I MEAN, THAT WAS
REALLY EMBARRASSING

189
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:10,949
WHAT HAPPENED
TO YOU.

190
00:08:12,075 --> 00:08:13,201
PHOEBE?

191
00:08:13,243 --> 00:08:14,869
YEAH?

192
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:18,332
PHOEBE, YOUR NOTE...
AMAZING.

193
00:08:18,373 --> 00:08:21,001
NOT ONLY DID NO ONE
TOUCH MY SANDWICH

194
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:24,254
BUT PEOPLE AT WORK ARE
ACTUALLY AFRAID OF ME.

195
00:08:24,296 --> 00:08:25,546
A GUY CALLED
ME "MENTAL."

196
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:28,633
"MENTAL" GELLER. YEAH.

197
00:08:28,675 --> 00:08:32,262
I'VE ALWAYS WANTED
A COOL NICKNAME LIKE THAT.

198
00:08:32,304 --> 00:08:34,806
YEAH, THE BEST YOU GOT
IN HIGH SCHOOL

199
00:08:34,848 --> 00:08:36,433
WAS "WET PANTS GELLER."

200
00:08:36,475 --> 00:08:38,435
IT WAS THE WATER FOUNTAIN,
OKAY?!

201
00:08:40,395 --> 00:08:41,896
ANYWAY...

202
00:08:43,023 --> 00:08:45,150
PEOPLE ARE WRITING REPORTS
FOR ME.

203
00:08:45,192 --> 00:08:48,403
UH, PUSHING BACK DEADLINES
TO FIT MY SCHEDULE.

204
00:08:48,445 --> 00:08:50,822
I'M TELLING YOU,
YOU GET TOUGH WITH PEOPLE

205
00:08:50,864 --> 00:08:53,574
AND YOU CAN GET
ANYTHING YOU WANT.

206
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:56,786
HEY, TRIBBIANI, GIVE ME
THAT COFFEE, NOW.

207
00:09:06,213 --> 00:09:07,839
THIS WAS REALLY FUN.

208
00:09:07,881 --> 00:09:11,634
I'VE BEEN WONDERING
IF YOU WERE EVER
GOING TO ASK ME OUT.

209
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:14,888
SO YOU, UH, STILL WONDERING?

210
00:09:14,929 --> 00:09:15,972
NO.

211
00:09:16,014 --> 00:09:17,265
WE JUST WENT OUT.

212
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:21,395
YOU'RE SMART.

213
00:09:21,436 --> 00:09:22,979
I LIKE THAT.

214
00:09:30,362 --> 00:09:32,322
OH, CANDLES.

215
00:09:34,324 --> 00:09:35,992
WHAT IS THAT,
A BLANKET?

216
00:09:36,034 --> 00:09:37,077
A VIDEO CAMERA?

217
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:38,078
OH, MY GOD!

218
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:40,121
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU THOUGHT

219
00:09:40,163 --> 00:09:44,792
YOU WERE GOING TO VIDEOTAPE US
HAVING SEX ON THE FIRST DATE.

220
00:09:50,257 --> 00:09:51,716
HI.

221
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:56,430
JOEY, IS WHAT SHE
JUST SAID, UM...

222
00:09:56,471 --> 00:09:58,014
OH, MY GOD.

223
00:09:58,056 --> 00:10:00,517
YOU WERE ACTUALLY
GOING TO...

224
00:10:03,562 --> 00:10:06,147
WHAT IS GOING ON HERE?

225
00:10:08,233 --> 00:10:10,777
AND WITH CHANDLER
IN THE NEXT ROOM?

226
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:12,070
WHAT, ARE YOU SICK?

227
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:18,868
I'M JOEY.

228
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:23,664
I MEAN, I'M DISGUSTING.

229
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:28,587
I MAKE LOW-BUDGET ADULT FILMS.

230
00:10:33,258 --> 00:10:35,176
HUH.

231
00:10:38,721 --> 00:10:39,973
YOU GUYS PROMISED

232
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:41,099
YOU'D BE MORE CAREFUL.

233
00:10:41,141 --> 00:10:42,601
I MEAN, COME ON,
THE GOOD JOEY NAME

234
00:10:42,641 --> 00:10:44,394
IS BEING DRAGGED
THROUGH THE MUD HERE.

235
00:10:44,436 --> 00:10:46,521
WE'RE SO SORRY.

236
00:10:46,563 --> 00:10:47,730
YEAH.

237
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:49,357
WELL, I'M TELLING
EVERYONE ABOUT YOU.

238
00:10:49,399 --> 00:10:50,733
IT'S THE ONLY WAY

239
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:52,651
TO EXPLAIN THE UNDERWEAR,
AND THE VIDEO CAMERA

